   "old": "- **Histogram quantization:** one 297 ps bin spans $3.0\\times10^8\\times297\\times10^{-12}/2=0.0446$ m of range, shown as 4.5 cm.",
   "new": "- **Histogram quantization:** one 297 ps bin spans $3.0\\times10^8\\times297\\times10^{-12}/2=0.0446$ m of range, shown as 4.5 cm. Equivalent-time sampling at 3 GHz gives bins of $1/(3\\times10^9\\ {\\rm s^{-1}})=333$ ps, which span $3.0\\times10^8\\times333\\times10^{-12}/2=0.050$ m.",
   "why": "Derivation for the IMX479 entry added to the table row."
  },
  {
   "id": "02_C0_parts1-9-008",
   "finding": "report #3 (PRF_ch); removing repetition",
   "old": "- **Unambiguous range:** $R_{\\rm amb}=c/(2\\,\\text{PRF})=3.0\\times10^8/(2\\times750\\times10^3)=200$ m at 750 kHz, and $3.0\\times10^8/(2\\times300\\times10^3)=500$ m at 300 kHz. $R_{\\rm amb}$ is the farthest range whose echo returns before the next pulse leaves (subsection 9 uses the same symbol); elsewhere $R_{\\max}$ means the maximum detection range.",
   "new": "- **Unambiguous range:** $R_{\\rm amb}=c/(2\\,\\text{PRF}_{\\rm ch})=3.0\\times10^8/(2\\times750\\times10^3)=200$ m at 750 kHz, and $3.0\\times10^8/(2\\times300\\times10^3)=500$ m at 300 kHz.",
   "why": "Relation uses the per-channel PRF of the symbol list; the R_amb definition sits in the symbol list and the paragraph under the table."
