  {
   "id": "02_C0_parts1-9-052",
   "finding": "report #31; report #34 (TI)",
   "old": "TI's ToF design guide gives $\\sigma_R\\propto c\\sqrt{n_e+n_T^2}/(n_m f_m C_d)$ [P, TI SBAU219D]. Here:",
   "new": "Texas Instruments' ToF design guide gives $\\sigma_R\\propto c\\sqrt{n_e+n_T^2}/(n_m f_m C_d)$ [P, TI SBAU219D], i.e. by Eq. (28) a phase noise $\\sigma_\\varphi\\propto\\sqrt{n_e+n_T^2}/(C_d\\,n_m)$. Here:",
   "why": "Ties TI's scaling to Eq. (28) as a phase noise and expands TI."
  },
